<title>GERMANY: Dresdner to offer Internet trading.</title>
<headline>Dresdner to offer Internet trading.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank AG said on Friday that it would begin today an Internet service to buy and sell stocks and bonds.</p>
<p>The Frankfurt-based bank said customers would need identification numbers as well as passwords to use the service, which sends orders in the form of electronic mail.</p>
<p>The Dresdner service is available at the Internet address http://www.dresdner-bank.de.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
